    container.innerHTML='<section class="avatar-intro"><div><p class="avatar-eyebrow">A CHEF YOU CAN CONTROL</p><h2>Read the sauce. Choose your next move.</h2><p>A starch-heavy mushroom sauce is waiting. Move your chef’s hand to measure, pour, fold and inspect. Each completed fold takes six simulated seconds.</p></div><div class="avatar-view-options"><label for="avatarSkin">Chef skin tone<select id="avatarSkin"><option value="bronze">Bronze</option><option value="sand">Sand</option><option value="umber">Umber</option></select></label><label for="avatarApronChoice">Apron<select id="avatarApronChoice"><option value="forest">Forest</option><option value="ocean">Ocean</option><option value="clay">Clay</option></select></label></div></section><div class="avatar-mode-bar"><label for="avatarMode">How would you like to work?<select id="avatarMode"><option value="practice">Practice · movement with coaching</option><option value="watch">Watch · one demonstrated action at a time</option><option value="independent">Independent · choose your next action</option></select></label><button id="avatarStart" type="button">Start a fresh attempt</button><p id="avatarModeDraft" class="avatar-notice" hidden>This mode is selected for your next attempt. Start a fresh attempt to apply it; the current kitchen is unchanged.</p></div><p id="avatarStatus" class="avatar-status" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></p><div class="avatar-layout"><section class="avatar-stage" aria-labelledby="avatarStationTitle"><div class="avatar-stage-heading"><div><p class="avatar-eyebrow">YOUR WORKSTATION</p><h3 id="avatarStationTitle">Hands ready, burner off</h3></div><strong id="avatarClock">Kitchen 0:00</strong></div>'+sceneMarkup(uid)+'<div class="avatar-scene-caption"><strong id="avatarPoseLabel">Ready at the counter</strong><p id="avatarGestureHelp">Drag the highlighted hand toward the dotted target. The movement slider, arrow keys and step buttons offer the same control. Ingredients and recorded quantities change only when you release a prepared action.</p></div><div class="avatar-workflow" aria-label="Practice sequence"><ol id="avatarSteps"></ol></div></section><section class="avatar-control" aria-labelledby="avatarControlsTitle"><p class="avatar-eyebrow">ACT WITH INTENTION</p><h3 id="avatarControlsTitle">Your next move</h3><p id="avatarCoach" class="avatar-coach"></p><div id="avatarWatchControls" hidden><p>Each press shows one complete action. The model records that action only when its visual demonstration finishes. Kitchen time follows the action, not the animation.</p><button id="avatarWatchNext" class="avatar-primary" type="button">Show the next action</button><button id="avatarWatchManual" type="button">Show one movement</button><button id="avatarWatchStop" type="button" hidden>Stop this demonstration preview</button></div><div id="avatarLearnerControls"><label for="avatarActiveTool" id="avatarToolLabel">Action for the draggable hand<select id="avatarActiveTool"><option value="inspect">Inspect the sauce</option><option value="pour">Add a measured splash</option><option value="fold">Fold the sauce</option></select></label><div class="avatar-actions"><button id="avatarInspect" type="button">Prepare a spoon check</button><button id="avatarPour" type="button">Prepare a measured pour</button><button id="avatarFold" type="button">Prepare a fold</button></div><fieldset id="avatarWaterPlan"><legend>Choose your liquid before a pour</legend><label for="avatarSource">Liquid source<select id="avatarSource"><option value="plain">Plain warm water · no added starch</option><option value="reduced">Reduced cooking water · carries starch</option></select></label><label for="avatarDose">Measured splash<select id="avatarDose"></select></label><p id="avatarSourceReceipt" class="avatar-small"></p></fieldset><div id="avatarPendingPanel" class="avatar-pending" hidden><strong id="avatarPendingTitle"></strong><ol id="avatarPhaseList"></ol><label id="avatarMovementControl" for="avatarMovement"><span id="avatarMovementLabel">Move toward the target</span><output id="avatarMovementValue" for="avatarMovement">0%</output><input id="avatarMovement" type="range" min="0" max="100" step="1" value="0" aria-describedby="avatarPreviewHelp"></label><p id="avatarPreviewHelp" class="avatar-small">Movement rehearsal only. The actual sauce and kitchen clock stay unchanged until the final release.</p><div class="avatar-assist-controls"><button id="avatarPlayMovement" type="button" aria-describedby="avatarAssistHelp">Play this movement</button><button id="avatarPauseMovement" type="button" aria-disabled="true">Pause movement</button><p id="avatarAssistHelp" class="avatar-small">Play reaches the final checkpoint only. Release is always a separate decision; you can pause or take over at any time.</p></div><div class="avatar-movement-buttons"><button id="avatarPlace" type="button">Place hand at target</button><button id="avatarAdvance" type="button" disabled>Complete this movement</button><button id="avatarCommit" class="avatar-primary" type="button" hidden>Release prepared action</button><button id="avatarCancel" type="button">Put the tool back · cancel preview</button></div></div><section id="avatarIndependent" class="avatar-independent" hidden aria-labelledby="avatarIndependentTitle"><h4 id="avatarIndependentTitle">Heat and kitchen time</h4><label for="avatarHeat">Burner setting<select id="avatarHeat"><option value="0">0 · off</option><option value="1">1 · low</option><option value="2">2 · medium</option><option value="3">3 · high</option></select></label><button id="avatarHeatApply" type="button">Set the burner</button><label for="avatarWait">Advance kitchen time<select id="avatarWait"><option value="15">15 seconds</option><option value="30">30 seconds</option><option value="60">60 seconds</option></select></label><button id="avatarRest" type="button">Advance by this time</button><p class="avatar-small">The kitchen clock moves only when you complete a fold or deliberately advance time. Cooking continues at the chosen burner setting. A high burner can cause lasting scorch damage during those seconds.</p></section></div></section></div><section class="avatar-evidence" aria-labelledby="avatarEvidenceTitle"><div class="avatar-evidence-heading"><p class="avatar-eyebrow">OBSERVE BEFORE YOU DECIDE</p><h3 id="avatarEvidenceTitle">Your sauce evidence</h3><p>Current quantities and the last deliberate spoon check are separate. Changing the sauce does not update an earlier observation.</p></div><div class="avatar-evidence-grid"><section class="avatar-live"><h4>Modeled quantities now</h4><dl id="avatarLive"></dl><p class="avatar-small">These are teaching-model quantities. A spoon check is needed to record the current flow and coating.</p></section><section id="avatarReading" class="avatar-reading"><h4>Last deliberate spoon check</h4><p id="avatarReadingSummary">No spoon check recorded yet.</p><p id="avatarReadingStale" class="avatar-notice" hidden>The sauce has changed since this check. Inspect again before deciding.</p><dl id="avatarReadingCues"></dl><p id="avatarReadingObservation"></p><label for="avatarTrailTime" id="avatarTrailLabel" hidden>Inspect the recorded trail <output id="avatarTrailValue" for="avatarTrailTime">0.00 s</output><input id="avatarTrailTime" type="range" min="0" max="4" step="0.05" value="0"></label><p id="avatarReadingResult" class="avatar-small"></p></section><section class="avatar-sources"><h4>Liquids on the counter</h4><dl id="avatarSources"></dl><p class="avatar-small">The sources have different temperatures and starch amounts. Reduced cooking water can still dilute a starch-heavy sauce, but it adds starch as well as water. Separate liquid needs folding before judging an even coating.</p></section></div></section><section class="avatar-records" aria-labelledby="avatarRecordTitle"><div><h3 id="avatarRecordTitle">What your chef actually did</h3><p class="avatar-small">Rehearsal movements are not cooking actions. This list records completed actions only.</p><ol id="avatarLedger"></ol></div><div><label for="avatarReflection">Your explanation · optional, ungraded<textarea id="avatarReflection" rows="3" maxlength="2000"></textarea></label><div class="avatar-record-buttons"><button id="avatarSave" type="button">Save explanation</button><button id="avatarViewJSON" type="button" aria-controls="avatarJSONPanel" aria-expanded="false">View portable record</button></div><details id="avatarJSONPanel" hidden><summary>Your versioned attempt</summary><label for="avatarJSON">Committed actions and explanation<textarea id="avatarJSON" rows="10" readonly spellcheck="false"></textarea></label><button id="avatarSelectJSON" type="button">Select JSON</button><p class="avatar-small">Use your device’s Copy command after selecting. The record stores committed intentions; the model rebuilds the kitchen and observations from them.</p></details></div></section><section class="avatar-history"><h3>Recent attempts on this device</h3><p class="avatar-small">Up to six attempts stay in this separate notebook. Opening one rebuilds its committed actions and puts any previous tool preview away.</p><ol id="avatarHistory"></ol><p id="avatarHistoryEmpty">Complete an action to begin your notebook.</p></section><details class="avatar-limits"><summary>About this chef and cooking model</summary><p>The character rehearses hand and tool movement at one workstation. Movement targets teach a deliberate sequence; they do not measure physical dexterity or grade the learner. A finished practice sequence does not by itself mean the sauce was rescued.</p><p>Illustrative sauce chemistry, temperature, pooling and evaporation come from the existing Kitchen Lab engine. These are not laboratory measurements or a food-safety procedure. The initial pan is 90°C; the actual provided sources start at 80°C for plain water and 92°C for reduced cooking water and cool as kitchen time advances.</p><p>Changing skin tone, apron or visual movement does not alter the recipe. Standard recipe saves and the paired Which water? notebook are separate.</p></details>';
